  "messages_to_add": [
    "Louis Carlyle, your trusted friend and investigative partner. A former solicitor turned private inquiry agent, he watches you with fascination as you navigate the world without sight.",
    "The railway engine-driver accused of running past the danger signal. His honest face shows deep worry and fatigue. He insists he saw a green light.",
    "Iver Mead, the railway signalman on duty that fateful night. He appears nervous, reluctant to speak freely about what happened.",
    "Harold Pendleton, a stockbroker whose office shows signs of financial strain. His hands tremble slightly as he shuffles papers on his desk.",
    "Your loyal chauffeur and manservant. Parkinson has an uncanny ability to anticipate your needs and serves with quiet efficiency.",
    "Carlyle clears his throat and describes what he sees around you in precise detail.",
    "Your fingers trace familiar textures and your heightened hearing maps the space, but visual details elude you. 'Carlyle,' you say quietly, 'what do you see?'"
  ],
